{"type":"standard","title":"Mitanni","displaytitle":"<span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Mitanni</span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q178665","titles":{"canonical":"Mitanni","normalized":"Mitanni","display":"<span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Mitanni</span>"},"pageid":140389,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Carte_du_Mitanni-en.svg/320px-Carte_du_Mitanni-en.svg.png","width":320,"height":233},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Carte_du_Mitanni-en.svg/490px-Carte_du_Mitanni-en.svg.png","width":490,"height":357},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1242111644","tid":"a4fd29d2-6285-11ef-b308-f52da569de51","timestamp":"2024-08-25T01:59:21Z","description":"Ancient Hurrian-speaking state in northern Syria and southeast Anatolia","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mitanni","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mitanni?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mitanni?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Mitanni"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mitanni","revisions":"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Mitanni","edit":"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mitanni?action=edit","talk":"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Mitanni"}},"extract":"Mitanni, earlier called Ḫabigalbat in old Babylonian texts, c. 1600 BC; Hanigalbat or Hani-Rabbat in Assyrian records, or Naharin in Egyptian texts, was a Hurrian-speaking state in northern Syria and southeast Anatolia with Indo-Aryan linguistic and political influences. Since no histories, royal annals or chronicles have yet been found in its excavated sites, knowledge about Mitanni is sparse compared to the other powers in the area, and dependent on what its neighbours commented in their texts.","extract_html":"<p><b>Mitanni</b>, earlier called <b>Ḫabigalbat</b> in old Babylonian texts, <abbr>c.</abbr><span> 1600 BC</span>; <b>Hanigalbat</b> or <b>Hani-Rabbat</b> in Assyrian records, or <span><i lang=\"egy\">Naharin</i></span> in Egyptian texts, was a Hurrian-speaking state in northern Syria and southeast Anatolia with Indo-Aryan linguistic and political influences. Since no histories, royal annals or chronicles have yet been found in its excavated sites, knowledge about Mitanni is sparse compared to the other powers in the area, and dependent on what its neighbours commented in their texts.</p>"}